andler is configured,\nthe error will be thrown from this method."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" handler is configured, errors will be caught and passed to the handler,\nand this method will return undefined."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The error state can be checked using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getErrorCount()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsExecuting()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"args","children":[{"type":"text","value":"args"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Parameters"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Awaited"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReturnType"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A promise that resolves with the function's return value, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"throws","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The error from the rate-limited function if no onError handler is configured"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const rateLimiter = new AsyncRateLimiter(fn, { limit: 5, window: 1000 });\n\n// First 5 calls will return a promise that resolves with the result\nconst result = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2');\n\n// Additional calls within the window will return undefined\nconst result2 = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2'); // undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useAsyncRateLimitedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(async (value: number) => { console.log(value) }, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\nvoid schedule(1)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useAsyncRateLimiter"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"args","text":"args","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"throws","text":"Throws","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":3},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/octane-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts#L37)\n\nReturns a stable rate-limited callback owned by the Octane lifecycle.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns the bound maybeExecute method with the wrapped function's parameter types. The returned Promise preserves the core result and error contract. A rejected rate-limit call resolves with undefined.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nUse useAsyncRateLimiter when you need selected state or control methods. This callback does not expose the utility, its store, or a child subscription.\n\nCall during component rendering. The hook retains its utility across renders and runs cleanup when the component unmounts.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`OctanePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/OctanePacerOptions.md)\\<[`OctaneAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/OctaneAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(...args): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nAttempts to execute the rate-limited function if within the configured limits.\nWill reject execution if the number of calls in the current window exceeds the limit.\n\nError Handling:\n- If the rate-limited function throws and no `onError` handler is configured,\n  the error will be thrown from this method.\n- If an `onError` handler is configured, errors will be caught and passed to the handler,\n  and this method will return undefined.\n- The error state can be checked using `getErrorCount()` and `getIsExecuting()`.\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### args\n\n...`Parameters`\\<`TFn`\\>\n\n### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the function's return value, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError\n\n### Throws\n\nThe error from the rate-limited function if no onError handler is configured\n\n### Example\n\n```ts\nconst rateLimiter = new AsyncRateLimiter(fn, { limit: 5, window: 1000 });\n\n// First 5 calls will return a promise that resolves with the result\nconst result = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2');\n\n// Additional calls within the window will return undefined\nconst result2 = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2'); // undefined\n```\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useAsyncRateLimitedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(async (value: number) => { console.log(value) }, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\nvoid schedule(1)\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseAsyncRateLimiter\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncRateLimitedCallback\ntitle: useAsyncRateLimitedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/octane-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts#L37)\n\nReturns a stable rate-limited callback owned by the Octane lifecycle.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns the bound maybeExecute method with the wrapped function's parameter types. The returned Promise preserves the core result and error contract. A rejected rate-limit call resolves with undefined.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nUse useAsyncRateLimiter when you need selected state or control methods. This callback does not expose the utility, its store, or a child subscription.\n\nCall during component rendering. The hook retains its utility across renders and runs cleanup when the component unmounts.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`OctanePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/OctanePacerOptions.md)\\<[`OctaneAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/OctaneAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(...args): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nAttempts to execute the rate-limited function if within the configured limits.\nWill reject execution if the number of calls in the current window exceeds the limit.\n\nError Handling:\n- If the rate-limited function throws and no `onError` handler is configured,\n  the error will be thrown from this method.\n- If an `onError` handler is configured, errors will be caught and passed to the handler,\n  and this method will return undefined.\n- The error state can be checked using `getErrorCount()` and `getIsExecuting()`.\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### args\n\n...`Parameters`\\<`TFn`\\>\n\n### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the function's return value, or undefined if an error occurred and was handled by onError\n\n### Throws\n\nThe error from the rate-limited function if no onError handler is configured\n\n### Example\n\n```ts\nconst rateLimiter = new AsyncRateLimiter(fn, { limit: 5, window: 1000 });\n\n// First 5 calls will return a promise that resolves with the result\nconst result = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2');\n\n// Additional calls within the window will return undefined\nconst result2 = await rateLimiter.maybeExecute('arg1', 'arg2'); // undefined\n```\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useAsyncRateLimitedCallback } from '@tanstack/octane-pacer'\n\n// During component rendering:\nconst schedule = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(async (value: number) => { console.log(value) }, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\nvoid schedule(1)\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseAsyncRateLimiter\n"}
